  "question": {
    "text": "An inductor of reactance $100 \\Omega$, a capacitor of reactance $50 \\Omega$, and a resistor of resistance $50 \\Omega$ are connected in series with an AC source of 10 V , 50 Hz. Average power dissipated by the circuit is ________ W.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{rms}} \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{rms}} \\cos \\phi \\\\ & \\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{rms}} \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{rms}}}{\\mathrm{z}} \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{\\mathrm{z}} \\\\ & \\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{rms}}^2 \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{\\mathrm{z}^2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{z}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{R}^2+\\left(\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{L}}-\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{C}}\\right)^2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{Z}=50 \\sqrt{2} \\Omega \\\\ & \\mathrm{P}=100 \\times \\frac{50}{2500 \\times 2}=1 \\mathrm{~W}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
